omx-panel (0.6.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * version 0.6.0
  * lv2-complement: two bundles that would share one complement name are both
    refused (plugin-hostd#218)
  * docs: the LV2 search order gives the same result at a different cost
    (plugin-hostd#218)
  * lv2-complement: a generated group node never merges into one already
    there (plugin-hostd#218)
  * lv2-complement: a bundle of ours no longer wanted is removed, not
    reported (plugin-hostd#218)
  * docs: the LV2 complement, what it writes and refuses, and where lilv sees
    it (plugin-hostd#218)
  * omx-complement-sync: the complement at install time, beside
    omx-modgui-sync (plugin-hostd#218)
  * lv2-complement: a replacing LV2 bundle with the inferred port groups,
    marked (plugin-hostd#218)
  * turtle-read: an absolute IRI is kept as written, only a relative one
    resolved (plugin-hostd#218)
  * check-spdx: the synthetic fixtures carry our header and are not exempt
    (plugin-hostd#218)
  * group-infer: a section word most names hold labels a numbered group; no
    label is emitted twice (plugin-hostd#218)
  * group-infer: one parameter repeated across sections is not a section
    (plugin-hostd#218)
  * docs: the 979-plugin figures after the numbering guard and the name
    labels (plugin-hostd#218)
  * docs: a generated group under a plugin's own priorities shows last, and
    why (plugin-hostd#218)
  * fixtures: omx-eq8 is the installed file again; the priority case is a
    synthetic fixture (plugin-hostd#218)
  * group-infer: MAX_GROUPS states what it is, a ceiling a 32-band EQ with
    its I/O does not fit (plugin-hostd#218)
  * group-infer: a numbered group's label comes from the names when they
    agree (plugin-hostd#218)
  * group-infer: a number pass groups only one numbering of one set of
    sections (plugin-hostd#218)
  * docs: the 979-plugin figures after the rule 3 and priority fixes
    (plugin-hostd#218)
  * group-infer: drop the group-of-one refusal, which no rule can reach
    (plugin-hostd#218)
  * fixtures: the Calf and MDA licences in SOURCES are their RPM tags in full
    (plugin-hostd#218)
  * group-infer: the doc lists every section word the module holds, and a
    test keeps it so (plugin-hostd#218)
  * group-infer: a plugin's own group keeps the display priority it states
    (plugin-hostd#218)
  * group-infer: a symbol's band number comes before a name's printed
    frequency (plugin-hostd#218)
  * LV2 group inference: the rules that find a plugin's port groups, as a
    pure function (plugin-hostd#218)
  * commit-message-check: the clean fixture cites this repository's own tool
  * commit-message-check: the SPDX licence line has its copyright line
  * commit-message-check: the fixture comment names no private repository
  * commit-message-check: the self-test fixtures are built from fragments
  * CI: the commit-message check is the commit-message-check action

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:32:14 +0000
